    "q-18643": {
      "dom_id": "step-q18643",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14196324/assets/ea0b899d48da746716c143eaa22e497250043a43ccc79b6662067f4046510613.png)\n\nConsider a right triangle inscribed in a semicircle of radius $3,$ as shown above. Find the maximum possible area of the triangle.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's call $l$ the length of one leg. By the Pythagorean theorem, the length of the other leg is $\\sqrt{36-{l}^{2}}.$\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is given by\n\n$$\nA(l)=\\frac{1}{2}l\\sqrt{36-{l}^{2}}\\,.\n$$\n\nSince $l$ is the length of a leg of a right triangle whose hypotenuse is $6$, the permitted range of $l$ is $0<l<6.$\n\nWe want to maximize $A(l),$ so we need to compute the critical points. Taking the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(l) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{36-{l}^{2}}-\\frac{{l}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{36-{l}^{2}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving $A(l)=0$ gives the following critical point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(l) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{36-{l}^{2}}-\\frac{{l}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{36-{l}^{2}}} & =0 \\\\ 36-{l}^{2}-{l}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {l}^{2} & =\\frac{36}{2} \\\\ {l}^{2} & =18 \\\\ l & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAll that's left now is to confirm that $l=3\\sqrt{2}$ does indeed give a maximum value of $A(l).$ To do this, we use the first derivative test. We write up a table of values:\n\n| Interval | $(0,3\\sqrt{2})$ | $3\\sqrt{2}$ | $(3\\sqrt{2},6)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $1$ | $$ | $5$ |\n| ${A}^{′}$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ |\n| $A$ | $↗$ | $\\text{max}$ | $↘$ |\n\nSo, $l=3\\sqrt{2}$ does indeed give a maximum, and the area of the resulting triangle will be the largest possible.\n\nFinally, the maximum possible area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(3\\sqrt{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{36-{(3\\sqrt{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
